Exec the Coot binary from the bin/coot wrapper.

Without exec, the process that starts bin/coot gets the pid of a /bin/sh
that waits on coot-1 (Linux) or MacCoot (macOS). Callers that track Coot
by that pid, such as phenix.agent, see the shell exit before Coot does.
With exec, the pid is Coot's. The exported LC_ALL, LANG and SYMINFO and
the exit status are unchanged.

--- a/coot/src/coot.in
+++ b/coot/src/coot.in
@@ -4,4 +4,4 @@
 prefix=@prefix@
 export SYMINFO=$prefix/share/coot/data/syminfo.lib
 exec_prefix=@exec_prefix@
-@libexecdir@/@COOT_BINARY_NAME@ "$@"
+exec @libexecdir@/@COOT_BINARY_NAME@ "$@"
